  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "identifier": "PREVAIL",
  "description": " PREVAIL is an R package designed to support dynamic, adaptable, and comprehensive transmission modeling for vaccine-preventable diseases (VPDs), particularly in crisis settings where routine immunization services are disrupted. Developed using the odin2 framework, PREVAIL enables stochastic, age-structured, and risk-structured disease transmission models that account for routine immunization, supplemental campaigns, and waning immunity. The package is tailored for humanitarian use cases, such as refugee settings or conflict zones, where the probability of outbreaks is high and intervention strategies must be robust and responsive. It includes flexible input handling, realistic population dynamics, and tools to project cases, attack rates, and impact of delayed or proactive vaccination campaigns. PREVAIL is supported by Community Jameel and builds on work funded by the FCDO for mortality rate modeling in Gaza.",
  "name": "PREVAIL: PRojection of Epidemics and VAccination Impact under Lapses in Coverage",
  "license": "https://spdx.org/licenses/MIT",
